 @Hardwareunboxed  But by how much it sucks right now? I might not be interested in raytracing, but want GPU which can support some of it if I happen to like game with raytracing effects. I also are recommending a friend to buy a GPU right now. He is a type which needs future proofing and does not care about raytracing. Do you see the pickle here? I need an GPU which can run RT games, but I do not care if it is good or not. When I look at AMD GPUs, I have no clue if I should just recommend RTX series or maybe AMD is good enough as it is. 

There is this grey line here, should he go with RTX 3080 or RX 6800 series. He won''t be using it for raytracing nor he cares about latest and greatest RT games or high FPS. However, he will expect to turn RT games on and he will want to play those games without issues.

This is why I think that while focus should not be on raytracing, I do believe that just 1 graph of an average game performance with raytracing on would be interesting and important enough to warrant its inclusion. Though, I understand that it is A LOT of extra work for little to show for and with next generation it won't matter anyways as RT will be included. It is just a small thing about what I thought when watching this video.

