 @AndyViant  I suspect Navi 21 and Navi 22 might already be out of production. 
Navi 33 seems to be planned for September and should still be on TSMC N7. N6 is just N7 with some EUV usage so we are talking about roughly the same production capacity. The problem is that it takes several months before a wafer is turned into a stack of video cards. If you now start a Navi 21 wafer, by the time the finished product is in stores, Navi 33 might be released. And if the rumors even hold a little bit of truth, Navi 21 and 22 would be instantly obsolete the moment Navi 33 arrives. Seeing as paper launching would look very bad for the next generation after the mess of the last two years, AMD should be motivated to order Navi 33 production on time. 

What I think AMD is doing it right now is clearing inventory. They facilitate their partners to sell off the remaining inventory with the old 16Gpbs and 18Gbps GDDR6. They do this partly because of shortages and partly because they want even more money for it. Because if they can get more from a 50XT model, they will prioritise that model. AMD could have easily said that the RX6600XT, RX6700XT and RX6900XT where EOL and replace those for the RX6650XT, RX6750XT and RX6950XT at the same price. They didn't do that and that is the cash grab here.
